WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:17.626
The nurse called Patrick's mom to pick him up from school.

2
00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:22.308
Back at home Patrick climbed into bed and slept until late the next morning.

3
00:00:23.268 --> 00:00:26.050
"That's one good thing about getting a stomach bug," he thought.

4
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.211
"Now I have the weekend to study for my math test!"

5
00:00:30.051 --> 00:00:31.812
And he had Slider to keep him company.

6
00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:36.155
The cat curled up near his feet, purring contentedly as Patrick studied.

7
00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:40.819
Two hours later Patrick's phone chirped.

8
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.163
He had a text from Dell: Feel up to some catch?

9
00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:47.765
Patrick stared at the words for a second.

10
00:00:48.325 --> 00:00:49.386
Then he started typing.

11
00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:51.968
Why did you tell Coach about my math test?

12
00:00:55.311 --> 00:00:55.911
Wasn't me!

13
00:00:56.572 --> 00:00:57.993
Probably your math teacher told him?

14
00:00:58.013 --> 00:01:01.416
"Oh," Patrick said out loud.

15
00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:02.872
That made sense.

16
00:01:03.112 --> 00:01:03.633
Of course.

17
00:01:04.693 --> 00:01:07.714
The teachers were supposed to inform Coach if an athlete was struggling.

18
00:01:08.574 --> 00:01:11.295
Patrick instantly felt bad about accusing his teammate.

19
00:01:11.915 --> 00:01:12.616
This was Dell.

20
00:01:13.196 --> 00:01:16.037
And Dell would never tell Coach about Patrick's math problems.

21
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:19.778
He typed his reply: At the park in 15.

22
00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:25.040
Dell was locking up his bike when Patrick arrived.

23
00:01:29.944 --> 00:01:32.505
They warmed up for a while, tossing the ball back and forth.

24
00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:37.226
"Coach was worried when you didn't show up for practice yesterday," said Dell.

25
00:01:37.246 --> 00:01:41.548
"I told him you had gone home sick and that we'd work together over the weekend."

26
00:01:42.228 --> 00:01:44.128
He stopped his windup and looked at Patrick.

27
00:01:44.148 --> 00:01:46.709
"You don't mind practicing today, do you?

28
00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.551
With the big game against the Hornets coming up, I figured—" "Of course I don't mind!"

29
00:01:52.891 --> 00:01:53.791
Patrick grinned at him.

30
00:01:53.812 --> 00:01:55.172
"Let's get busy."

31
00:01:56.704 --> 00:01:59.805
Patrick relaxed as the ball whizzed into his glove over and over.

32
00:02:01.505 --> 00:02:04.046
It felt great to be playing baseball, catching with Dell.

33
00:02:05.126 --> 00:02:07.867
But he still didn't feel ready to face the rest of the team yet.

34
00:02:08.807 --> 00:02:12.408
He'd acted like a jerk the other day and assumed everyone was laughing at him.

35
00:02:13.388 --> 00:02:16.029
He'd also been making a lot of mistakes on the field lately.

36
00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:20.890
By now he was sure everyone liked Mickey a whole lot more than they liked him.

37
00:02:22.491 --> 00:02:25.332
Around dinnertime Daniel opened Patrick's bedroom door.

38
00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:29.826
"Dad said he'd drop us off at Mickey's for a team pizza party.

39
00:02:30.406 --> 00:02:31.487
Be ready in a half hour."

40
00:02:31.507 --> 00:02:33.568
"A team pizza party?"

41
00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:35.770
Patrick stared down at his math book.

42
00:02:36.751 --> 00:02:38.432
"Uh I'm not going."

43
00:02:39.312 --> 00:02:41.374
"What?" Daniel stepped into the room.

44
00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:45.636
"Dude, it's a team party.

45
00:02:46.217 --> 00:02:49.979
It's like a pep rally, a bonding thing for the whole team before the big game against the

46
00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:53.562
Hornets." "I'm still sick," Patrick lied.

47
00:02:54.122 --> 00:02:55.143
Daniel gave him a look.

48
00:02:55.723 --> 00:02:56.544
"No, you're not."

49
00:02:57.564 --> 00:03:01.706
"Anyway, Mickey is everybody's favorite new player," Patrick blurted out.

50
00:03:02.547 --> 00:03:03.507
"Nobody will miss me."

51
00:03:04.768 --> 00:03:08.010
He lifted Daniel's old mitt, which was lying on the floor next to his bed.

52
00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.932
"You can take this mitt back.

53
00:03:11.372 --> 00:03:12.693
I think the magic's gone."

54
00:03:14.153 --> 00:03:16.315
Daniel took the mitt and slipped his hand inside.

55
00:03:16.335 --> 00:03:19.796
"It's not magic, Patrick.

56
00:03:20.297 --> 00:03:22.798
It's just another dumb baseball superstition.

57
00:03:23.639 --> 00:03:25.720
But you don't need magic or superstitions.

58
00:03:26.568 --> 00:03:27.689
I have confidence in you."

59
00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:30.290
Patrick blinked in surprise.

60
00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.092
"Then why do you criticize everything I do?"

61
00:03:34.152 --> 00:03:34.893
Daniel shrugged.

62
00:03:34.913 --> 00:03:37.414
"I guess I am a little tough on you."

63
00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.155
"A little tough?"

64
00:03:39.715 --> 00:03:40.516
Patrick echoed.

65
00:03:40.536 --> 00:03:41.816
"You're brutal!

66
00:03:42.857 --> 00:03:47.019
When Dell and I didn't pick off that base runner, you made a really big deal of it—in

67
00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.140
front of the whole team.

68
00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.121
I felt like an idiot."

69
00:03:51.081 --> 00:03:53.503
"Look, this is my first coaching job.

70
00:03:54.063 --> 00:03:55.684
I want to do a good job for Coach.

71
00:03:56.876 --> 00:04:01.798
Plus, I've been pushing you hard because I wanted you to get the starter position—and keep it."

72
00:04:01.818 --> 00:04:04.019
"Well, I lost it."

73
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.881
"I'm sorry for being hard on you," Daniel went on.

74
00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:10.522
"And who knows how the rest of the season will go.

75
00:04:11.502 --> 00:04:14.543
My guess is that sometimes you'll catch, and sometimes Mickey will catch.

76
00:04:15.504 --> 00:04:17.404
But tonight isn't about you or me.

77
00:04:17.945 --> 00:04:18.865
It's about the team."

78
00:04:19.785 --> 00:04:21.206
He tossed the mitt onto the bed.

79
00:04:21.226 --> 00:04:23.987
"The mitt is yours.

80
00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.008
And you should go to the pizza party.

81
00:04:27.008 --> 00:04:30.130
That's what team players do—they support their team."

82
00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.172
"Okay," Patrick mumbled.

83
00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.495
He hung his head as he headed for the shower a minute later.

84
00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:41.658
right," he thought.

85
00:04:42.198 --> 00:04:45.221
Patrick had been thinking about himself—instead of his team.

86
00:04:45.241 --> 00:04:49.143
"Thanks for the ride, Dad," said Daniel.

87
00:04:49.163 --> 00:04:51.265
"Yeah," said Patrick.

88
00:04:51.285 --> 00:04:53.326
"I'm glad you drove us in your car.

89
00:04:53.766 --> 00:04:55.928
It's embarrassing to ride around in Mom's van."

90
00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:57.917
Mr. Deboe laughed.

91
00:05:00.238 --> 00:05:01.979
"That van isn't too comfortable either.

92
00:05:02.959 --> 00:05:04.780
But it's good advertising for your mom.

93
00:05:05.541 --> 00:05:10.463
She's wanted to start this business for a long time, and taking the van to games and practices

94
00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.264
is a small way we can support her."

95
00:05:13.305 --> 00:05:15.946
"It's like taking one for the team," said Daniel.

96
00:05:17.047 --> 00:05:18.388
"Exactly," said Mr.

97
00:05:18.408 --> 00:05:21.309
Deboe. Patrick felt horrible.

98
00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:26.052
He'd been so embarrassed about the van, he hadn't thought about Mom for one second.

99
00:05:27.208 --> 00:05:30.210
Of course, she attracted new clients with that crazy van.

100
00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.252
It was definitely time for him to stop feeling sorry for himself.

101
00:05:34.272 --> 00:05:39.615
"Woof!" he said as he climbed out of the car.

102
00:05:39.635 --> 00:05:42.196
"Team Deboe is on the go!"

103
00:05:43.177 --> 00:05:44.117
"That's the spirit!"

104
00:05:44.478 --> 00:05:45.138
said his father.

105
00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:51.061
When Mickey saw Daniel and Patrick approaching the house, he flung open the front door.

106
00:05:51.081 --> 00:05:54.283
"Hey, guys!"

107
00:05:54.903 --> 00:05:55.804
He looked at Patrick.

108
00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.841
"I wasn't sure you were coming."

109
00:05:58.601 --> 00:06:00.602
"Stomach flu," mumbled Patrick.

110
00:06:00.622 --> 00:06:03.023
"The Deboes are here!"

111
00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.003
Mickey called to the rest of the team.

112
00:06:05.484 --> 00:06:11.106
"We've got one assistant coach and a survivor of the cafeteria's 'Friday Special!'"

113
00:06:12.126 --> 00:06:15.268
He raised Patrick's hand like a boxer as some kids cheered.

114
00:06:19.709 --> 00:06:21.730
barely survived," joked Patrick.

115
00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:25.992
"Yeah, the cafeteria food is horrible in middle school," said Buck.

116
00:06:26.828 --> 00:06:30.049
Daniel went to get some pizza while Patrick stood awkwardly with Mickey.

117
00:06:30.069 --> 00:06:33.490
"Where's your dog?"

118
00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.470
he asked, trying to make conversation.

119
00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.991
"Ratty's outside, showing off."

120
00:06:38.471 --> 00:06:39.992
Mickey pulled back a window curtain.

121
00:06:42.092 --> 00:06:44.873
Patrick saw Todd throwing a ball for the dog to fetch.

122
00:06:44.893 --> 00:06:48.734
"Looks like Ratty's found a friend."

123
00:06:48.754 --> 00:06:52.795
"Ratty's been lonesome since my brother left for college.

124
00:06:53.615 --> 00:06:54.756
I'm more of a cat person."

125
00:06:55.852 --> 00:06:56.773
"Really? You like cats?"

126
00:06:57.233 --> 00:06:57.814
said Patrick.

127
00:06:57.834 --> 00:07:02.017
"Yeah. Like I said the other day, cats are cool.

128
00:07:02.518 --> 00:07:05.420
They're calm, thinking creatures but ready to pounce."

129
00:07:06.421 --> 00:07:08.583
"Kind of like catchers," said Patrick.

130
00:07:09.764 --> 00:07:12.646
"Exactly!" The two catchers did a fist bump.

131
00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.369
"Sorry about the other day," Patrick said.

132
00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:17.770
Mickey shrugged.

133
00:07:18.391 --> 00:07:19.191
"No problem.

134
00:07:20.152 --> 00:07:22.074
You're going to make it to the Hornets' game, aren't you?"

135
00:07:23.055 --> 00:07:24.476
"Sure." Patrick nodded.

136
00:07:25.004 --> 00:07:26.345
"We're going to need a good hitter.

137
00:07:26.986 --> 00:07:28.267
I bet Coach will start you."

138
00:07:29.328 --> 00:07:30.228
Mickey shook his head.

139
00:07:30.248 --> 00:07:31.509
"No way.

140
00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.351
You and Dell are true partners.

141
00:07:34.131 --> 00:07:35.713
It's like you read each other's minds."

142
00:07:36.613 --> 00:07:39.196
Then he waved for Patrick to follow him to the family room.

143
00:07:39.216 --> 00:07:40.256
"Come on.

144
00:07:40.717 --> 00:07:43.439
It's time to get this team pumped up for the game!"
